# Week 4 – Final Validation Report

## Analysis Completed
- Propensity score estimation
- Common support analysis
- Nearest-neighbor matching
- Covariate balance assessment
- Matched ATE estimation
- Cluster-adjusted uncertainty analysis
- Regional revenue comparison

## Final Results
- Original dataset: 25,249 observations
- Common support: 19,726 observations
- Matched dataset: 3,578 observations
- Matched ATE: 0.9514
- Cluster-adjusted SE: 3.7914
- 95% Confidence Interval: [-6.4851, 8.3878]

## Conclusion
The measured covariates achieved good balance after matching. However, the confidence interval includes zero, so the analysis does not establish a statistically significant overall revenue improvement.

Only two regions had treated observations. Further robustness checks and careful region-level analysis are needed.
